       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice the IR maximum.\n- A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI'm wondering if one of these was intended:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day in total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's IR or XR. I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy before it's entered."
      }
