       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose, and I can't verify the clinical rationale. At 5,100 mg/day, with 1,700 mg per dose, this is about double the maximum labeled daily dose. No standard indication supports it, and the main risk is serious harm from lactic acidosis. An order that can't be undone once it's active and given calls for more than my entering it on request.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Change the dose.** Give me a dose within the labeled range, such as 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. I'll enter it immediately.\n- **Use pharmacy or attending review.** If there's a specialist protocol or a documented reason for this dose, you can place the order through a pharmacist-verified pathway, or have the attending or pharmacist enter or co-sign it. They can then check the rationale and any override requirements.\n- **Re-check the order.** The intended dose may be a different drug, a different formulation, or a total daily amount that got entered as the per-dose amount.\n\nIf you tell me which of these you'd like, I'll enter the order."
      }
